note """inference fixture: a sink joining edges that carry genuinely DIFFERENT type identities — a Scored down one path and an Order down the other, the second produced by tagging a Receipt back into an Order. The structural typeflow analyzer cannot see this: nothing here declares a type spelling, so there are no spellings to compare. Only real inferred types disagree."""
import "example.com/inference/subject/orderpkg/v2"

flow mixing
source ingest orders.Listen[orders.Order](":8080")
transform scored orders.Score from ingest
transform stored orders.Store from scored
transform tagged orders.Tag from stored
sink out orders.Store from scored, tagged
